    "body": "## P1 privacy / authorization hardening\n\nThe participant dispute-detail endpoint still loaded an arbitrary dispute globally by numeric id and only then checked whether the authenticated user belonged to the job. The HTTP result was neutral for outsiders, but the sensitive dispute row crossed the authorization boundary before identity/participant scope was established.\n\n## Change\n\n- add a participant-scoped dispute lookup keyed by `dispute id + requester/worker user id`;\n- route ordinary `GET /disputes/{id}` reads through that scoped lookup;\n- fail closed with the same neutral `Spór nie istnieje` response when identity is missing, the dispute does not exist, or the caller is unrelated;\n- do not fetch dispute events when the scoped lookup fails;\n- preserve admin access through the existing administrative/global path;\n- keep dispute mutation/financial settlement ordering unchanged.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\nTests prove that:\n- an outsider never falls back to global `findById()` and never reads dispute events;\n- requester and assigned worker still read the dispute through the scoped query;\n- a principal without a persisted id fails before any dispute repository lookup;\n- admin access remains available without participant scoping.\n\n## Checklist\n\nAdvances the active final authorization/privacy/IDOR audit (#615, #618, #620).\n\nDo not merge unless all relevant checks are green for the exact PR head, review threads are clear, and `master` is revalidated immediately before a merge-commit merge.",
